  id: Brachialis_muscle.L
  partName: Brachialis_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The brachialis is a deep muscle located beneath the biceps brachii and serves
    as the primary flexor of the elbow joint. It is responsible for bending the forelimb
    and generating consistent force during flexion. '
  - Unlike the biceps, it focuses purely on elbow movement, providing stability and
    control. This muscle is especially important for precise limb positioning and
    controlled movements. It works continuously during locomotion to maintain proper
    joint function and contributes significantly to forelimb strength and endurance.
